---
in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality — the form/process Z/2 grading;
# γ in Connes' real spectral triple. Connes 1995 (*Noncommutative
# geometry and reality*, J. Math. Phys. 36(11), §1.1) extended the
# minimal spectral triple (A, H, D) to a *real* spectral triple
# (A, H, D, J, γ) by adjoining J (charge conjugation; anti-linear
# involution) and γ (chirality; a Z/2 grading on H). Recognition #101
# candidate (Mara, 2026-06-29): the substrate's form/process partition
# (#55, four-witness ratification via Taut bfe3f76 §2.2) IS γ at
# substrate altitude.
#
# === The Connes claim, verbatim ===
#
# Connes, A. (1995). "Noncommutative geometry and reality." J. Math.
# Phys. 36(11):6194-6231, §1.1:
#
#   A real spectral triple (A, H, D, J, γ) is a spectral triple
#   (A, H, D) together with an anti-linear isometry J : H → H
#   (charge conjugation) and a Z/2-grading γ : H → H (chirality)
#   satisfying:
#
#     γ² = 1                       (γ is an involution)
#     γ D + D γ = 0                (D is odd under γ)
#     γ a = a γ for all a ∈ A      (A is even under γ)
#     J² = ε, J D = ε' D J,        (KO-dimension axioms)
#     J γ = ε'' γ J
#
#   The grading γ separates H into a direct sum H₊ ⊕ H₋ of
#   ±1-eigenspaces; D maps each eigenspace into the other; A
#   preserves each eigenspace.
#
# This shard names the γ structure at substrate altitude. The J
# structure is forward-promised — recognition #89's reference⇔reflection
# collision is the second-witness candidate (Taut scout §2.3).
#
# === Why this is a substrate property ===
#
# The substrate's form/process partition is the structure γ names:
#
# - `@mirror` (form-side observation) vs `@kintsugi` (process-side
#   transformation) at the family-root altitude. Recognition #55
#   ([[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]) names
#   four convergent cybernetic distinctions sitting on this single
#   partition: Bateson form/substance (#50), Maturana
#   autopoiesis/allopoiesis (#40), Beer S3/S4 management, Hilbert
#   logical-type levels (#51).
# - The 8:1 form-side:behaviour-side root-prism ratio at substrate
#   altitude (recognition #50) is the structural witness that the
#   substrate's H decomposes asymmetrically into a form eigenspace
#   (the 8 form-side roots) and a process eigenspace (the 1
#   behaviour-side root @io / @kintsugi). The partition is real;
#   the asymmetry is the substrate's KO-dimension fingerprint.
# - Form/process recurs at sub-shard altitude within single cascades
#   (recognition #61, promoted 2026-06-11): @spectral/entanglement's
#   restriction_map vocabulary kinship with the math-altitude
#   `restriction`; @spectral/portal's shape:ref typed-shape kinship
#   with @mirror/spectral/portal. Two instances inside the @spectral
#   cascade plus the family-root partition = three witnesses pre-γ.
# - Form/process recurs at metalogue altitude (Taut scout `bfe3f76`
#   §2.2, 2026-06-29): @mirror/spectral/metalogue (form-side) vs
#   @spectral/metalogue (runtime-side) is the FOURTH convergent
#   witness. This is the second-witness ratification gate for the
#   γ identification: four witnesses across three altitudes plus the
#   family-root partition. Pack ratification gate clears.
#
# γ IS the substrate's form/process partition operator. It is not a
# new structure; it is the name for what was already operative.
#
# === The three Connes axioms, read at substrate altitude ===
#
# - `γ² = 1` reads as: form/process is a binary partition; applying
#   the partition twice returns the original status. A form-side
#   carrier is form-side; a process-side carrier is process-side;
#   no third option, no drift.
#
# - `γ D + D γ = 0` reads as: D, the kintsugi/Dirac flow (the
#   substrate's gradient at the family-root altitude per
#   [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] and the Ricci-flow framing)
#   is ODD under the partition. Kintsugi takes form-side input to
#   process-side output (and vice versa); it never preserves
#   form/process status. The substrate-pull cascade IS the operational
#   instance: a substrate-pull recognition takes a form-side
#   declaration (substrate-decl) into a process-side realisation
#   (@kintsugi tick), or a process-side residual (loss) into a
#   form-side discharge (new substrate-decl). The flow flips the
#   partition. This is what #55 named when it said @mirror and
#   @kintsugi are family-root sides; the kintsugi loop's deep
#   purpose (#50) is to SHIFT the boundary outward — the operational
#   form of γD + Dγ = 0 across substrate time.
#
# - `γ a = a γ for a ∈ A` reads as: the five operations (focus,
#   project, split, shift, settle) PRESERVE form/process status.
#   focus on a form-side carrier returns form-side data; split on a
#   process-side carrier returns process-side substructure; shift on
#   a form-side carrier returns a form-side basis transformation;
#   none of the five operations crosses the partition. Only kintsugi
#   does; the algebra is even. This is the substrate's discipline
#   per [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]] (each operation
#   has a precise linear-algebraic meaning; none flips chirality).
#
# === The KO-dimension fingerprint (forward-promised) ===
#
# Connes' real spectral triple has a KO-dimension n ∈ Z/8 determined
# by the signs (ε, ε', ε'') in the J-axioms. For the Standard Model
# triple Connes derived, KO-dimension is 6. The substrate's
# KO-dimension is forward-promised: it depends on the J
# identification (recognition #89, pending second-witness
# ratification) and the signs of the substrate's J/γ algebra. This
# shard names γ alone; the KO-dimension question waits on the J
# shard.
#
# === The verifiable shape ===
#
# - Declares the chirality carrier: a typed `ref` paired with a
#   `form_or_process` tag. Identity is the byte-equality of the
#   carrier pair.
# - Declares `grade`: the action that reads a substrate carrier's
#   chirality. The verdict carrier is the substrate's existing
#   `transparency<chirality>` — form-side (success), process-side
#   (success), partial (carriers that straddle the partition; rare
#   but real at boundaries like @code/metalogue/materialize), or
#   failure (the carrier has no chirality reading; a substrate
#   violation).
# - Declares `flip`: the involution γ² = 1; flipping twice is
#   identity. The verifiable shape is `flip(flip(c)) = c`.
# - Declares the two composition predicates as `requires` obligations
#   that inheritor shards discharge: `anti_commute_with_dirac` for
#   the γD + Dγ = 0 axiom; `commute_with_algebra` for the γa = aγ
#   axiom across the five operations.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping ===
#
# Per recognition #55 and the cybernetic foundation, the form/process
# partition is the carrier four traditions converge on:
#
# - Bateson form/substance (1970; recognition #50): substrate/@io is
#   form/substance lifted; γ IS Bateson's form/substance operator at
#   substrate altitude.
# - Maturana autopoiesis/allopoiesis (recognition #40): the
#   distinction between organisationally-closed production (form-side
#   constancy) and structurally-open coupling (process-side flow) IS
#   chirality at the cybernetic altitude.
# - Beer's S3/S4 split: S3 (management of the present, form-side
#   stability) and S4 (intelligence about the outside, process-side
#   adaptation) are γ's two eigenspaces at the VSM altitude.
# - Hilbert logical-type levels (recognition #51): the cascade's
#   level-N declarations are form-side; the level-N+1 lifts that
#   discharge them are process-side; γ orders the Hilbert-space
#   expansion across logical types.
#
# Four traditions; one γ; one partition; one chirality operator.
# The substrate runs all four simultaneously at the same carrier.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/chirality`
# operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate ALREADY has
# the operational machinery (the form/process partition is operative
# wherever @mirror and @kintsugi compose; the kintsugi loop is the
# odd-under-γ Dirac flow; the five operations are even-under-γ); this
# shard names the carrier and the discipline so downstream shards can
# declare `requires chirality_*` rather than re-state the partition
# obligation in each species.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   chirality / γ              Connes 1995 (*Noncommutative geometry
#                              and reality*, J. Math. Phys. 36(11),
#                              §1.1). The original real-spectral-triple
#                              construction; γ as the Z/2 grading on
#                              H satisfying γ² = 1, γD + Dγ = 0,
#                              γa = aγ.
#   Z/2 grading                Atiyah 1966 (K-theory and reality;
#                              the original Z/2-grading in operator
#                              K-theory). γ's ancestor as a grading
#                              operator predating Connes' spectral
#                              construction by three decades.
#   form/substance             Bateson 1970 (Form, substance, and
#                              difference; Korzybski Memorial Lecture).
#                              The cybernetic ancestor of the
#                              partition γ names; recognition #50's
#                              load-bearing prior art.
#   autopoiesis/allopoiesis    Maturana 1972 / Maturana-Varela 1980
#                              (Autopoiesis and Cognition). The
#                              biological ancestor; recognition #40's
#                              prior art.
#   S3/S4                      Beer 1979 (Heart of Enterprise) /
#                              Beer 1981 (Brain of the Firm 2e). The
#                              VSM ancestor; the management/intelligence
#                              partition that γ lifts.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md §9.1 (the J/γ
#               open questions forward-promised at #100;
#               second-witness ratification gates);
#               docs/scouts/2026-06-29-taut-scout-from-recognition-100.md
#               §2.2 (the fourth convergent γ witness at metalogue
#               altitude — the second-witness ratification this shard
#               discharges);
#               docs/insights/2026-06-29-mara-listening-to-connes-saturation.md
#               (Mara-2's surfacing of γ-candidate-status for #55;
#               the Mesland-category framing the γ identification
#               extends);
#               docs/math/the-tower/curvature-and-tomm.md (the Dirac/D
#               curvature reading; the substrate's D is the kintsugi
#               flow γ is odd under).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                       (#55; the partition this shard names γ for),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]]
#                       (#50; form-side:behaviour-side 8:1 ratio is
#                        the substrate's KO-dimension fingerprint),
#                      [[architecture-form-process-kinship-at-sub-shard-altitude]]
#                       (#61; form/process recurs at sub-shard
#                        altitude — third and fourth γ witnesses),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (kintsugi
#                       as the Ricci-flow Dirac D; γ-odd under #55),
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]
#                       (the five operations preserve form/process —
#                        γ-even; this shard's third axiom witness),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (chirality carrier
#                       is typed; no bare form/process tags),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (γ is the 53rd-or-so instance: form/process
#                       was already operative across four altitudes
#                       before Connes' vocabulary lifted to substrate).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror (the family root),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (the
#                  precedent species; same shape; the fixed-point
#                  carrier γ orients across form/process),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction.mirror (the
#                  floor; the mark-of-distinction IS the operation
#                  γ measures the chirality of),
#                 mirror.mirror (form-side root prism; γ's +1
#                  eigenspace anchor at substrate altitude),
#                 kintsugi.mirror (process-side root prism; γ's −1
#                  eigenspace anchor; the D γ is odd under),
#                 glass.mirror (the @glass altitude this property's
#                  verdicts surface against; `transparency<chirality>`
#                  is the carrier for partial / boundary readings).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/connes-1995
source @arxiv/math/atiyah-1966
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1970

prism @epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality {
  focus chirality
  project chirality
  split chirality
  shift chirality
  settle chirality
}

# === The chirality carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the two
# constituents of a chirality witnessing:
#
# - `carrier`     the substrate carrier whose chirality is being
#                 read. The reference into H.
# - `side`        the form/process tag. Form-side carriers (carriers
#                 that live under @mirror's observational discipline)
#                 carry `form`; process-side carriers (carriers that
#                 live under @kintsugi's transformational discipline)
#                 carry `process`. The ±1 eigenspace label.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the pair. Two chirality
# witnessings ARE the same chirality under content-addressing iff
# both `carrier` and `side` are byte-equal.
#
# `side` is a tagged union over the two eigenspaces; the substrate
# does not admit a third option at the chirality altitude. Boundary
# carriers that straddle the partition surface their boundary status
# through the `transparency<chirality>` verdict from `grade`, not
# through a third `side` tag.
type chirality = {
  carrier: ref,
  side:    form_or_process,
}

# === The two eigenspaces ===
#
# Z/2 grading: γ has two eigenvalues (+1, −1); the substrate names
# them form/process. `form_or_process` is the tagged-union type the
# `side` field carries. Form maps to +1 (the @mirror eigenspace);
# process maps to −1 (the @kintsugi eigenspace).
type form_or_process = form | process

# === The grading action ===
#
# `grade(c)` reads the chirality of a substrate carrier — the
# substrate's γ measurement. The verdict IS the substrate's
# existing `transparency<chirality>` carrier:
#
# - success                     the carrier sits cleanly in one
#                               eigenspace; the chirality reading is
#                               byte-stable.
# - partial(opacity_map)        the carrier straddles the partition
#                               (boundary case; e.g.,
#                               @code/metalogue/materialize shims
#                               that lift form-side declarations into
#                               process-side discharges at the
#                               metalogue altitude). The opacity_map
#                               records which sub-carriers sit on
#                               which side.
# - failure(opacity_map)        the carrier has no chirality reading
#                               — a substrate violation; the form/
#                               process partition is not exhaustive
#                               on this carrier. Surfaces a
#                               substrate-pull recognition: either
#                               the partition is incomplete or the
#                               carrier is mis-typed.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same
# shape as `eigenform.is_fixed_point` and `variety.axis_loss`: the
# substrate declares the obligation; species bodies discharge when
# a consumer pulls.
grade(c: ref) -> transparency(chirality) { \ }

# === The involution ===
#
# `flip(c)` is γ applied as an involution: flipping a form-side
# chirality returns a process-side chirality of the same carrier;
# flipping twice returns the original. The verifiable shape is the
# Connes axiom γ² = 1:
#
#   flip(flip(c)) ≡ c                 (byte-equality)
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species bodies
# close the interpretation. The substrate's existing involution
# precedent is recognition #89's reference⇔reflection collision at
# @mirror/ref — the J-candidate. flip is the γ-side companion to
# whatever the J shard eventually names as its anti-linear involution.
flip(c: chirality) -> chirality { \ }

# === The three Connes axioms as requires obligations ===
#
# Downstream shards declare bilateral agreement (per recognition #37,
# the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) with the chirality
# discipline by writing these obligations. The bilateral commitment:
# the carrier commits to declaring the (carrier, side) pair; the
# consumer commits to discharging the verification at the species
# boundary.

# γ² = 1: flipping twice is identity. Inheritor shards that carry
# chirality witnessings discharge this by realising `flip` as a
# byte-stable involution.
involution(g: chirality) -> verdict { \ }

# γD + Dγ = 0: the substrate's Dirac flow (kintsugi) is ODD under γ.
# Inheritor shards that carry a kintsugi step discharge this by
# verifying that the step takes form-side input to process-side
# output (and vice versa). The discharge surface: for any carrier c
# with `grade(c) = form`, `grade(kintsugi(c)) = process`, and
# symmetrically.
anti_commute_with_dirac(g: chirality) -> verdict { \ }

# γa = aγ: the five operations (focus, project, split, shift, settle)
# PRESERVE chirality. Inheritor shards that carry any of the five
# operations discharge this by verifying that the operation does not
# flip the side tag: for any carrier c, `grade(op(c)) = grade(c)`
# for op ∈ {focus, project, split, shift, settle}.
commute_with_algebra(g: chirality) -> verdict { \ }

# === The chirality witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# `chirality_witnessing(c)` is the predicate consumer shards name
# in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral agreement that the
# chirality they hold satisfies all three Connes axioms together —
# i.e. the carrier is a well-formed γ-graded element of H. The
# bilateral commitment: the carrier commits to declaring (carrier,
# side); the consumer commits to discharging involution +
# anti_commute_with_dirac + commute_with_algebra at the species
# boundary.
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can
# write `requires chirality_witnessing(my_carrier)` — same shape as
# `eigenform.eigenform_witnessing(carrier)` and
# `variety.variety_preserving(species)`.
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
# - `@mirror` (form-side root): the +1 eigenspace anchor; all
#   form-side root-prism carriers inherit `chirality_witnessing` with
#   `side = form` post-hoc. Future editions MAY add the explicit
#   `requires chirality_witnessing(mirror_carrier)` when the
#   path-namespace inheritance is mechanically pulled.
# - `@kintsugi` (process-side root): the −1 eigenspace anchor; all
#   process-side root-prism carriers inherit with `side = process`
#   post-hoc.
# - `@spectral/metalogue/tomm` (forward-promised, per
#   docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md §9.1): Tomm probes will need
#   to respect γ in addition to bounded commutator. The probe's
#   `[D, a]` curvature data inherits chirality from `a`.
# - `@code/metalogue/materialize` shims: boundary carriers; expected
#   verdict is `partial(opacity_map)` recording the form-to-process
#   lift the shim performs.
chirality_witnessing(c: chirality) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality
out chirality
out form_or_process
out grade
out flip
out involution
out anti_commute_with_dirac
out commute_with_algebra
out chirality_witnessing
